  All three options also add a failing count to the heading, e.g. [38;5;153mproduction: 10 services, 3 failing health checks, as [39m
  [38;5;153mof …[39m, and keep the snapshot's row order (an existing test locks that in). It's easy to switch between options later,
  unless something already parses the current output.

  [1mMy recommendation is B.[0m It answers "which ones are failing, and on what" at a glance and keeps one row per service.
